+# Independent numerical integrity references
+
+These original synthetic SI cases freeze the independently reviewed analytical basis of C-N1/M03-INTEGRITY-v1. `generate.py` uses only Python's standard library; no production assembler, section, solver, or result enters expected values. Decimal precision is 100 digits; Machin's arctangent identity generates pi with an omitted-term margin below 1e-105. Decimal strings preserve reference precision in `fixtures.json`. They are numerical approximations to the named exact expressions, not certified intervals.
+
+Run reference checks with `python3 test_reference.py`. Regenerate with `python3 generate.py`; a change to frozen bytes requires review. This verifies executable reference consistency and deliberate negative controls; it does not demonstrate product correctness. A first self-check exposed default Decimal context rounding in the J=2I assertion; the assertion now explicitly uses the generator's 100-digit context. No physical comparison tolerance changed.
+
+`cargo run --manifest-path Cargo.toml` is a source-prepared observation executable. It prints JSONL input and actual product envelopes for both existing solver modes, plus generic dense/sparse matrix observations. It makes no passing assertions. Execution is withheld until the manager grants the shared build lane. Generic `solve_dense` is an auxiliary nonsymmetric API; its acceptance of N07 is an observation, not itself a failure of that API. The required new structural gate is a separate typed contract.
+
+## Exact basis and applicability
+
+A=pi(OD²-ID²)/4, I=pi(OD⁴-ID⁴)/64, J=2I, E=200 GPa, G=80 GPa, OD=0.2 m, ID=0.18 m. Therefore EA=380000000*pi N, EI=1719500*pi N m², GJ=1375600*pi N m². Tip bending follows EI w''=F(L-x), zero root displacement/slope; tip torsion follows theta=T L/GJ. N01 is an Euler–Bernoulli model check at L/D=10, not a negligible-shear claim; N09 is its L/D=50 companion. All cases are static small-displacement constant-section passive elasticity. No buckling, follower load or material-nonlinear claim follows.
+
+The N02 common rotation (3/5,4/5,0) is a physical null motion when translations are fixed; RX intersects it and RZ does not. N04's separate free body adds six null modes. N05/N06 have exact torsion equations k theta_root=T and a(theta_tip-theta_root)=T, a=687800*pi. They are physically stable for positive k regardless of magnitude. NP-A decodes the EXACT binary64 a, fl(a+k), and T separately with Decimal.from_float. It solves those stored equations independently, retaining both intended and represented answers. N05's stored increment is 214748*2^-31; intended-answer relative error exceeds 1e-9 even for the exact stored solution. N06 loses its positive contribution entirely. These are assembly-resolution issues, not physical mechanisms. The stored residual is evaluated at 100 digits and is not asserted identically zero after finite Decimal rounding.
+
+NP-B is C=I+cS+cS², K=CCᵀ; every frozen load is K times the independently selected all-ones displacement. For c=3/4, the published derivation bounds kappa2(K)<429 independently of dimension, while the absolute inverse recurrence grows exponentially. `z_squared_u` records what happens IF a certificate uses delta>=2^-53; an exact factor residual can be zero for dyadic data. This fixture never falsely asserts an actually evaluated certificate failed. The c=0.750000000001 companion remains positive by invertible C; the 429 bound is not claimed without a separate perturbation bound. Permutations are explicit index maps; later probes must permute K, f and recovered u coherently.
+
+NP-C is explicitly a synthetic connector generalized-coordinate seam, not an authored pipe model: six restrained rigid coordinates coexist with one free internal slip. NP-D's skew and nonfinite matrices are intentionally inadmissible injection controls. Contact lift-off data are a two-mode linearized seam; a real product active-state witness remains pending.
+
